WEBVTT

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:12.660
I believe in you, Kyo. We'll meet again.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:28.470
How? It's impossible!

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:38.310
Oil-free canned tuna again?

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:42.520
Just eating that stuff all
the time isn't a balanced diet.

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:44.290
I balance it.

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:46.860
This is an extra helping of protein.

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:49.600
I'll eat a real meal when
I get home, so quit worrying.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.220
I never said I was worried.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:53.500
No luck today, either.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:55.090
Where is this mysterious babe of yours?

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:59.030
They said we haven't had a transfer
student in two or three years.

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:02.180
We've searched and searched
and there's no sign of her.

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:03.730
You sure you didn't just dream her?

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:06.440
She's not a dream!

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:10.370
You saw it yourself! How my home
flashed with light, and then...

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:13.420
You keep saying that,
but I don't know what you mean.

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:15.280
But, after it happened, I!

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:18.250
I was led by Shizuno Misaki...

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:21.260
Rode in that shining robot...

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:23.430
And then...

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:25.590
It's impossible!

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:28.260
Yeah, impossible. But, I...

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:30.470
The memories <i>feel</i> real.

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:33.600
Please, save this world.

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:36.880
I have a ton of questions to ask her!

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:39.670
Topping the list being why she disappeared!

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:42.920
Maybe you've been looking
so hard for a model...

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:45.020
for your swim club P.R. video
that you imagined her.

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:46.450
I didn't imagine her!

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:52.630
Just supposing that I believe you,

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:55.420
are you sure you can
trust your own memory?

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:59.800
I don't think this sketch of her
face is going to help us find her.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:02.260
It's a general idea of her, okay?
A <i>general</i> idea!

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:12.610
Don't you guys start
disappearing on me, too!

00:04:33.670 --> 00:04:36.370
Sogoru, you still have some time left.

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:38.130
Shouldn't you check it over?

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:41.170
In my case, the hardest
questions aren't on the exam.

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:47.270
Whoa! Excellent!

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:05.760
Hold it!

00:05:07.670 --> 00:05:08.130
Wait!

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:10.030
I said wait...

00:05:12.170 --> 00:05:13.610
What?

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:15.100
Um... Sorry.

00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:27.120
So, you're still looking
for this phantom girl?

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:29.220
Tell me what's wrong.

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:32.520
Wait, don't tell me it's <i>that.</i>

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:34.630
Do you want to show them?

00:05:34.630 --> 00:05:37.430
How hard you're working
to resurrect the swim club?

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:39.870
It's not about that!

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:41.460
Then what is it about?

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:49.680
<i>This video is coming from</i>
<i>Lu-shen on his recon mission.</i>

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:53.510
<i>It's very rare for us to</i>
<i>discover a new deutera zone.</i>

00:05:54.610 --> 00:05:57.620
The core still hasn't been def-terraformed.

00:05:57.620 --> 00:05:58.610
And Zegatank?

00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:03.520
The Caladrius is currently 3,000
to the rear of Zegapain Garuda.

00:06:04.390 --> 00:06:06.520
Have them get a Q.L. charge from Zegatank.

00:06:06.890 --> 00:06:08.450
Prolong the recon mission time.

00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:09.520
Roger!

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:21.410
Transferring 500 Q.L. to Zegapain Garuda.

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:22.070
<i>Much obliged!</i>

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:38.480
Q.L. charge, complete.

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:40.080
Continuing recon.

00:06:40.490 --> 00:06:43.550
<i>Zegatank, returning to ship.</i>
<i>Good luck out there.</i>

00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:49.700
Our lack of Cerebrants
is clearly a serious problem.

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:51.800
Shouldn't we at least reinstate the boy?

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:54.260
You support Shizuno's idea, then?

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:57.280
Her interference has
had a destabilizing effect...

00:06:57.280 --> 00:06:59.910
on the environmental systems
in the Maihama server!

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:02.310
Yehl's activity authorization
runs out in one hour.

00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:08.220
In short, it's too soon to be talking
about recovering a new meta-body.

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:11.650
Meeting adjourned!

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:19.190
Anyway, feel free to come see
me if anything's troubling you.

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:21.130
Right! Will do!

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:26.370
Like I said!

00:08:02.980 --> 00:08:05.580
I wonder where Sogoru went.

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:07.550
Whatcha doing, Ryoko?

00:08:07.850 --> 00:08:10.180
Mizuki, have you seen Kyo?

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:12.650
Sogoru? No, I haven't seen him,

00:08:12.650 --> 00:08:14.980
but I saw the three stooges
headed for the pool before.

00:08:15.350 --> 00:08:17.460
Man, it's almost indecent!

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:19.080
Yeah, indecent!

00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:20.920
What're you getting at?

00:08:20.990 --> 00:08:23.300
Well, your club's about to be shut down.

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:26.400
But you're just running around
chasing some phantom girl's ass!

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:28.090
So, what's it to you?!

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:32.770
Kawaguchi... Give it a rest.

00:08:32.770 --> 00:08:34.740
Back off, he's been asking for this!

00:08:36.040 --> 00:08:37.530
You don't know how to fight!

00:08:42.650 --> 00:08:44.920
What's he so mad about?

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:46.910
It's a grudge from middle school.

00:08:47.090 --> 00:08:47.780
Why, you!

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:55.560
Let's go!

00:09:00.630 --> 00:09:02.830
He <i>let</i> me hit him!

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:06.870
So, I guess swimming's the only
thing he really cares about, huh?

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:09.800
You gotta admit,
he made good time on that lap.

00:09:10.180 --> 00:09:11.800
That was on purpose?

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:15.880
They say it's Sogoru's fault
that the team was broken up.

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:18.720
The medley relay team.

00:09:19.150 --> 00:09:21.050
He took all the blame for it himself.

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:23.180
No matter how hard it was for him...

00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:28.960
I don't get it. Where are you?!

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:30.390
Shizuno Misaki!

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:35.890
It's open!

00:09:52.750 --> 00:09:57.450
There's lots of them. Is it because
we're so near to the deutera zone?

00:09:57.860 --> 00:09:59.760
The sensors aren't working.

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:01.820
The Ulvorfuls are jamming them!

00:10:02.230 --> 00:10:05.250
<i>Time remaining for recon:</i>
<i>26 minutes, 30 seconds.</i>

00:10:05.630 --> 00:10:09.400
It's all happening again!
And we just sit and gnash our teeth...

00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:11.670
May-yen, holonic shield!

00:10:11.770 --> 00:10:13.570
Wha? R- Right!

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:30.660
Lu-shen!

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:33.590
<i>No problem. The Garuda's fast</i>
<i>enough to let me dodge them.</i>

00:10:33.790 --> 00:10:35.730
We only just got that thing tuned up!

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:38.030
<i>Then this is a good chance to</i>
<i>let me get a feel for piloting it!</i>

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:40.600
Shizuno, are you there?

00:10:40.600 --> 00:10:41.570
<i>Yes.</i>

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:43.030
This isn't getting us anywhere.

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:44.700
So, we gamble again?

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:46.070
<i>I think so.</i>

00:10:46.610 --> 00:10:48.940
I don't care if you inform the commander of this.

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:53.880
If I weren't an A.I., I could
physically stop you, however...

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:58.040
I see that Kyo Sogoru
has opened the doorway himself.

00:10:59.950 --> 00:11:03.150
<i>Forward! I want to keep moving forward!</i>

00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:33.940
Would you do it again for me?

00:11:34.090 --> 00:11:37.290
Shizuno Misaki?!
Wh-Wh-Where are your clothes?!

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:41.250
You promised me, didn't you?
To save the world.

00:11:41.990 --> 00:11:44.190
In exchange for me
being in your P.R. video?

00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:50.170
<i>Shift to Cerebrant mode!</i>
<i>Commence replication check!</i>

00:11:50.170 --> 00:11:54.370
<i>Data comparison shows 0.6% C.H.I.P. loss.</i>

00:11:54.370 --> 00:11:57.010
<i>Dry damage detected in left-side</i>
<i>abdominal and facial regions.</i>

00:11:57.010 --> 00:11:58.870
<i>Suitable for self-regeneration.</i>

00:12:10.090 --> 00:12:11.890
Where are we?

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:15.560
Aboard a Cerebrum flying carrier: the Oceanus.

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:17.130
Oceanus... Agh!

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:18.760
Wh-wh-what am I wearing?!

00:12:19.430 --> 00:12:23.040
So, you're saying this is Zegapain's hangar, huh?

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:25.730
Man, this game's realistic!

00:12:28.910 --> 00:12:31.310
<i>Huh? What's the student</i>
<i>council president doing here?</i>

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:33.800
I don't recall authorizing a transmission.

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:38.620
Lu-shen requested backup.

00:12:38.620 --> 00:12:41.140
How can we ignore a
fellow member of Cerebrum?

00:12:41.990 --> 00:12:43.460
Cerebrum?

00:12:43.460 --> 00:12:45.750
It's our name. The name of our team.

00:12:46.690 --> 00:12:48.160
I'm begging you as well!

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:51.600
At this rate, Lu-shen and May-yen
won't make it back alive!

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:54.760
I don't buy this act.

00:12:56.940 --> 00:13:00.100
You expect to rehabilitate him this way?
But can he handle this?!

00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:04.770
<i>It's not a question of "can I!" I've already</i>
<i>cleared the first level, Mr. President!</i>

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:07.410
I am not "the president."

00:13:07.410 --> 00:13:11.140
Here, I am an officer of Cerebrum,
commander of the Oceanus.

00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:13.710
<i>What?! Are you high?!</i>

00:13:14.290 --> 00:13:17.790
He thinks this is all a game!
Never mind the danger of a transmission!

00:13:17.790 --> 00:13:21.660
He doesn't understand that he's risking
his life if he doesn't make it back in time!

00:13:22.930 --> 00:13:25.560
I don't suppose we could just
ask him to understand that.

00:13:26.500 --> 00:13:28.300
Are we approaching the deutera zone?

00:13:28.300 --> 00:13:29.300
Aye.

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:33.310
Ricerca, specify the transmission point.
Don't hit the Garuda.

00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:33.910
Aye, sir.

00:13:33.910 --> 00:13:35.240
Commander!

00:13:35.610 --> 00:13:37.480
What did they mean by "dangerous?"

00:13:37.480 --> 00:13:39.070
Now moving to transmission chamber.

00:13:47.390 --> 00:13:51.580
<i>Initiating countdown. Transmission scatter</i>
<i>rate confirmed and compensated for.</i>

00:13:52.020 --> 00:13:53.890
<i>Confirm release of chamber seal.</i>

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:55.990
<i>Q.L. driver, conjunction!</i>

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:08.100
<i>Gunner and Wizard I.D.s, locked in.</i>

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:09.710
<i>Stand by for meta-body transmission!</i>

00:14:13.050 --> 00:14:17.040
<i>Now moving into chamber.</i>
<i>Transmission zone scanning, complete.</i>

00:14:17.220 --> 00:14:20.990
<i>E.X. condition, green. All clear.</i>

00:14:20.990 --> 00:14:23.160
<i>Bednorz parameters, stable.</i>

00:14:23.160 --> 00:14:25.190
<i>Bednorz curve, holding!</i>

00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:27.090
<i>Transmission scatter rate, green.</i>

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:29.560
<i>Compensating for</i>
<i>materialization probability flux.</i>

00:14:29.560 --> 00:14:31.930
<i>Restoration coordinates,</i>
<i>set and locked!</i>

00:14:31.930 --> 00:14:35.370
<i>Transmission port, energy compilation at 98%.</i>

00:14:35.670 --> 00:14:37.570
<i>Now moving into transmit position.</i>

00:14:39.340 --> 00:14:40.670
<i>Releasing hangar locks.</i>

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:46.550
<i>Zegapain, teleport!</i>

00:14:46.550 --> 00:14:47.810
Roger.

00:14:47.810 --> 00:14:48.640
Entangle!

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:52.110
That's what I say, right?

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:55.750
<i>Transmission chamber, operating normally.</i>

00:14:55.750 --> 00:14:58.160
<i>Q.L. flow rate: 5.0852.</i>

00:14:58.160 --> 00:14:59.820
<i>Within tolerances.</i>

00:15:16.210 --> 00:15:19.010
<i>Altair transmission, complete.</i>

00:15:30.560 --> 00:15:33.430
<i>Zegapain Altair: transmission, complete.</i>

00:15:33.430 --> 00:15:34.290
Let's do this!

00:15:47.470 --> 00:15:49.630
Ulvorfuls still closing.

00:15:57.250 --> 00:15:58.510
Over there?

00:16:02.050 --> 00:16:04.060
Why are you flying us
into the middle of them?

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:06.350
First, we draw the enemy off.
Gun, please!

00:16:07.060 --> 00:16:10.390
Front grip weapon chamber coil output, okay.

00:16:11.100 --> 00:16:14.120
Holonic field, forming.
Holonic launcher! Right hand!

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:20.360
Incoming!

00:16:34.750 --> 00:16:39.210
The Ulvorfuls are moving away.
It's Kyo Sogoru.

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:41.150
How well will he do?

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:47.960
You're not hitting them!

00:16:48.700 --> 00:16:50.330
Is it happening again?!

00:17:05.820 --> 00:17:06.950
Deutera reaction!

00:17:06.950 --> 00:17:07.610
It's close.

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:13.460
Ulvorfuls: wiped out.

00:17:15.660 --> 00:17:16.630
Aanvals, closing.

00:17:19.460 --> 00:17:20.930
More enemies coming, huh?!

00:17:20.930 --> 00:17:23.200
We don't have much Q.L. left for the launcher.

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:24.200
No problem!

00:17:30.540 --> 00:17:31.880
What are you planning?

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:33.450
In a fight, get in your opponent's face!

00:17:33.450 --> 00:17:34.510
Don't be ridiculous!

00:17:34.510 --> 00:17:36.670
I am serious! Starting now.

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:01.600
Out of ammo? Gimme the sword! No, wait!

00:18:07.680 --> 00:18:09.270
You're pissin' me off!

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:22.130
That reckless!

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:25.930
Thanks to him, we got to see
them building their nest.

00:18:26.360 --> 00:18:29.500
Structure of deutera zone
now ascertained.

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:30.590
All right! We're returning to the ship!

00:18:34.010 --> 00:18:37.480
It's over. Entangle, time out.

00:18:37.480 --> 00:18:39.110
Stage two is cleared, huh?

00:18:41.780 --> 00:18:44.310
You... kissed me, before. Why?

00:18:45.720 --> 00:18:48.780
Because that's the sort of
relationship we have.

00:18:54.890 --> 00:18:58.350
We can use him as he is.
As a decoy, at least.

00:19:26.630 --> 00:19:29.430
Okay, camera's rolling!

00:19:29.430 --> 00:19:33.300
And three, two, one... Action!

00:19:41.810 --> 00:19:46.010
Isn't she great?! Isn't she? Huh?
Huh? That's the swim club for you!

00:19:46.340 --> 00:19:48.310
That's Shizuno Misaki, the senior, right?

00:19:48.310 --> 00:19:50.850
She's straightlaced, but fills
out that swimsuit really nice!

00:19:50.850 --> 00:19:53.650
Misaki-sempai, you're so cool!

00:19:53.650 --> 00:19:55.990
Why does everyone know about her?

00:19:55.990 --> 00:19:57.620
What are you talking about?

00:19:57.620 --> 00:20:00.680
She's become famous since she
transferred here a week ago!

00:20:00.830 --> 00:20:02.830
Naturally, considering how pretty she is.

00:20:02.830 --> 00:20:05.000
What are you all talking about?!

00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:06.570
A week ago?!

00:20:06.570 --> 00:20:08.470
We've been looking for her
the whole time, and... Huh?

00:20:10.870 --> 00:20:14.640
The cosmological constant
has been stabilized, right?

00:20:14.640 --> 00:20:16.730
Right, and there're no problems
in the system, either.

00:20:17.780 --> 00:20:21.210
Hey, Mr. President, you'll stop
my club being shut down, right?

00:20:21.210 --> 00:20:23.320
Looks like I'll be getting
some new members.

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:26.880
Um, sure! If you get more members,
I'll consider it.

00:20:29.450 --> 00:20:31.080
Why's he so happy?

00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:35.390
You think it's beginning?
The rebirth of the swim club?

00:20:35.390 --> 00:20:37.020
Yeah, it's begun.

00:20:38.260 --> 00:20:40.930
Misaki-sempai,
can you smile for me, please?

00:20:49.940 --> 00:20:52.100
<i>Yes. It's begun.</i>

00:20:58.380 --> 00:21:00.010
Sempai? Over here, please.

00:21:10.630 --> 00:21:12.690
<i>Things are finally starting to move.</i>

00:22:51.530 --> 00:22:55.060
No way! There's a game
that's called Zegapain?!

00:22:55.370 --> 00:22:58.370
So, why am I so good at it
when I've never played before?

00:22:58.370 --> 00:23:01.610
And what's with this secret message?

00:23:01.610 --> 00:23:05.280
There's so much stuff I don't understand,
my head feels like it's about to explode!

00:23:05.280 --> 00:23:07.210
But the thing I don't
understand the most...

00:23:07.210 --> 00:23:13.750
is me and why I've been unquestioningly
getting used to fighting these battles.

00:23:13.750 --> 00:23:17.260
Next time, on Zegapain: "Deutera Zone."

00:23:17.260 --> 00:23:19.490
My thoughts, never to be erased.
